  "key_finding": "Under matched conditions (n=1500, same seed, same \u03b5=0.05), the discrepancy is fully explained by two factors: (1) Soft vs hard metric \u2014 hard argmax gives ~2-5x larger apparent reduction than the soft plan cost for the SAME Sinkhorn solution; (2) Non-standard priors \u2014 'empirical' and 'uniform' \u03b5 are much closer to the data, reducing random pairing cost by ~10x and inflating % reduction. The gaussian-prior soft-metric number (Test 2's exact methodology) is the relevant one for ELF's actual training setup."
